# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs. It is shared by all
# three stages — `source`, and through it `test` and `build` — so what is dropped
# here is dropped from the tests as well as from the build.
#
# `node_modules` and `.git`: the Go build resolves modules through `go mod
# download` against the committed `go.sum`, and `node_modules` is not read by
# anything the image does. It is also the largest thing in this tree, and copying
# it in on every build is the cost this line exists to avoid.
node_modules
.git
.gitignore
.github
coverage
coverage.*
*.lcov

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# Docs, the gate's own scripts and the files that describe the image. None of it
# is read by the binary, by `go vet` or by `go test`, so none of it needs to be in
# the context — and `Dockerfile` and `docker-compose.yml` in particular are read
# by Docker and by compose, not by the build, which is why excluding them here is
# not the build error it would be if a stage tried to `COPY` one.
#
# THE NEGATIONS THAT USED TO BE AT THE BOTTOM OF THIS FILE ARE GONE, and their
# removal is the point rather than a tidy-up. They existed because `pins.test.ts`
# reads four of these files and the Bun test stage could not copy a path the
# context had dropped. The image is built on Go now, the Go test stage copies the
# whole context, and no Go test in this repository reads a file at the repository
# root — `internal/sessiontest/guard_test.go` and `internal/sessionredis` walk
# `cmd/` and their own packages, and that is the whole of it. So the exclusions
# stand without an exception list, which is the state where the list cannot go
# stale: a file added here is dropped, and a Go test that later needs it fails
# loudly with "no such file" rather than running without it.
#
# What replaced the tripwire, for the record, is `test/dockerStage.test.ts`'s
# check on the COPY list — retired, because the test stage is `COPY . .` now and
# two of its assertions were about that list while the other two had become
# tautologies on it. The property it held is asserted where the image can be seen:
# the CI `image` job diffs the `*_test.go` files the built image holds against
# `find`. A Go-side local half — this file, read the way `dockerStage.test.ts` read
# the Dockerfile — is not written yet, and `HANDOFF-cutover-01.md` says so.
#
# `src/` and `test/` are deliberately NOT here: `internal/equivalence` reads
# `test/equivalence/reference.ts` and stands it up, so the TypeScript tree is in
# the context until that harness retires with it.
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CHANGELOG.md
cafaye.yml
bin
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile